    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39-a3">

                <pb facs="0138" n="54" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg54"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 325.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Baiz.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-01-12"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 12,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with my letter to you of the
                    7th instant, I have now to apprise you of the receipt of a communication from
                    the Acting Secretary of the Treasury, of the 9th instant, saying that his
                    Department will use all legal endeavors, through its collectors of customs, to
                    prevent any violation of the neutrality laws on the part of any individuals
                    against the Republic of Honduras.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
